; Binds `(big n)` to `:impl "wasm:huge"` — the sibling double.wasm
; exports `huge` as a function that returns a frame header claiming
; a ~4 GiB payload that doesn't exist. Hosts MUST cap the reported
; length before allocating mirror buffers (spec §9.3); the rejection
; surfaces as `plugin_func_alloc_failed` at the call span.
(plugin :name double :version "1.0.0"
  (expr-func :name big
    :arity (fixed 1)
    :params [number]
    :result number
    :impl "wasm:huge"))
